\code{sig.level} is allocated to each tail.

For \code{exact.method = "midp"}, the lower and upper mid-p tails at an
observed count \eqn{x} are, respectively,
\deqn{P_0(X < x) + \tfrac{1}{2}P_0(X = x)}
and
\deqn{P_0(X > x) + \tfrac{1}{2}P_0(X = x).}
